html+='</section>';
html+=`<section><h1>Teacher-only answers and review</h1><p class="status">Engineering checks are not educator approval. Current status: ${currentRevision(m,s)?.revision.status??'unregistered'}.</p><h2>Answer key</h2><div class="answer"><p>Worked example:30°+90°=120°;180°−120°=60°.</p><p>Second worked example:56°+85°=141°;180°−141°=39°.</p><p>Guided practice:56°+82°=138°;180°−138°=42°.</p><p>Fresh check:24°+57°=81°;180°−81°=99°.</p></div><h2>Why this is a new check</h2><p>The example, guided question and check are different problems, and the two assessed answers differ. Moving the diagram does not create an attempt or mastery record. The live question flow still uses the existing grader and evidence rules.</p><h2>Decisions for the educator</h2><ol><li>Correctness: verify the angle sum, parallel construction and all arithmetic.</li><li>Prior knowledge and clarity: can the learner identify each interior angle and explain a straight angle?</li><li>Conceptual explanation: can the learner explain why the parallel line copies A and B, rather than claim that dragging proves the theorem?</li><li>Worked steps: can the learner explain why both known angles are added and subtracted from 180°?</li><li>Task alignment: do the guided and independent third-angle questions assess the teaching?</li><li>Unsupported claims: keep measurement distinct from proof and synthetic browser success distinct from demonstrated learning.</li></ol><p>Decision: □ revision required □ blocked □ eligible for educator approval through the authorised review process. Reviewer/name/date/notes:</p><div style="height:40px;border-bottom:1px solid #aaa"></div></section>`;
html+=`<section><h2>Scope and provenance</h2><p>Module: ${m.competency}<br>Strategy: ${s.id}</p><p><code>${contentHash(m.competency,s)}</code></p><p>Example:gen:ahtri:30,90<br>Guided:${s.guided}<br>Independent:${s.check}</p><p>Interaction is explicitly opt-in with the geometry-lab build flag. A non-test default build keeps the static representation. Existing research flags, educational approval gates and answer records are preserved.</p><p>JSXGraph 1.14.3 is used under its MIT licence, with the licence retained in the repository. Geometry uses planar Euclidean triangles; the movable example restricts C to above the fixed base. It does not demonstrate every possible triangle orientation.</p><p>The broader milestone separately tests an explicitly consented learner→educator→fresh-check return, denial/revocation and repeat/reload. No automatic mastery or educational approval follows from educator resolution.</p><p>Preserved calculus limitation: some follow-up questions use radical/rational first-principles forms after a quadratic explanation. This remains a teacher task-alignment decision; it is not silently claimed fixed here.</p></section></body></html>`;
